+//! Answers browser sessions: what a `zeo-browser` sidebar, through `zeo-browser-host` and the
+//! devtools bridge, may do to agent threads (story 045, design.md §B2).
+//!
+//! The bridge hands every session to [`handle_session_message`] and ends it with
+//! [`close_session`]. A session is approved before anything else: an identity
+//! (`<browser>:<extension_id>`) never seen before is asked about in the most recently active
+//! window, with Allow and Deny. Allow is remembered across restarts in the key-value store,
+//! under [`APPROVED_CLIENTS_KEY`]; Deny refuses that identity for the rest of the run; nobody
+//! answering within [`APPROVAL_TIMEOUT`] refuses the session. [`RevokeBrowserAccess`] forgets
+//! every approval and closes every session.
+//!
+//! Every line logged here carries an event, a session id, the browser and a sanitised extension
+//! id, and fixed codes: never message text, entry text, page content or a URL (R13.4).
+
+use std::collections::HashSet;
+use std::fmt;
+use std::sync::Arc;
+use std::sync::atomic::{AtomicU64, Ordering};
+use std::time::{Duration, Instant};
