+// Story 045, task 7.2 — approving a browser before it can read or drive threads (design.md §B2
+// Approval). Requirements: R4.1–R4.7, R13.1 (its log line is checked by Q15's grep). Q4.
+// Fixtures and seams: `test_support` (support.rs header).
+//
+// Hostile halves first (identity is `<browser>:<extension_id>`):
+//   - wrongly COLLAPSE: approving `chrome:approved-ext` approves neither `chrome:approved-exu`
+//     (another id) nor `firefox:approved-ext` (another browser);
+//   - wrongly SPLIT: the same identity with another extension_version is still approved;
+//   - deny is per identity: a denied identity is refused at once, another identity still asks;
+//   - the 120 s timeout: still pending at 119 s, refused after 120 s.
+
+use std::time::Duration;
+
+use gpui::TestAppContext;
+use serde_json::json;
